{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":97019,"duration_api_ms":88699,"num_turns":20,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9fed60a5-d6cf-4c8e-9e59-d0333d6f8909","total_cost_usd":0.7127557499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creation_input_tokens":55825,"cache_read_input_tokens":566689,"output_tokens":3218,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":55825,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":11,"outputTokens":3218,"cacheReadInputTokens":566689,"cacheCreationInputTokens":55825,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7127557499999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"evidence":["All 17/17 reproduction_factors tests pass: temperature suppression, instability, condition, density (monotonic), TAN/NO2 (independent), egg-dropping (AND assertion), stressor compounding, named parameter tunability, extracted-knob behavior, 2000-hour stable breeding (3+ completed hatch cycles via ShrimpHatched events), neglected-tank stall (final <= initial), snapshot suppression labels, density observability, immediate density suppression, mineral suppression, default toxic full-suppression preservation.","Full tank_core test suite passes: 0 failures across 30 test binaries (~430 total tests). Full tank_data (39 tests), tank_scenarios (40+5 tests), tank_harness (38 tests) all pass with 0 failures.","cargo clippy -p tank_core -- -D warnings passes clean. cargo fmt --all --check passes clean.","Working tree is clean for tracked project files: git diff --name-only HEAD returns only .claude/worktrees/tanksim-6e5.4.7 (infrastructure, not deliverable).","reproductive_readiness_factors() computes all 8 named factors: temperature, condition, minerals (GH), stability, molt_stress, density, tan, nitrite — each backed by species parameters in neocaridina_davidi.toml and ShrimpRuntimeParams struct.","temp_condition_factor() uses named parameters: temp_condition_min_factor (clamp floor), temp_condition_low_divisor_c, temp_condition_high_divisor_c. The temp_condition_min_factor is correctly excluded from the strictly-positive preset validation list (line 1005 now starts with ca_min_mg_per_l) while remaining in the non-negative+finite check (line 913) and the runtime check_unit_interval invariant (invariants.rs:466-468).","ShrimpHatched event defined in EventKind enum (events.rs:20) and emitted during successful clutch resolution (shrimp.rs:981). test_mature_stable_tank_breeds_well requires hatched_events >= 3 for completed reproductive cycles.","TankSnapshot exposes repro_dominant_suppression field (snapshot.rs:67) via dominant_repro_suppression_label() which reports the minimum factor label when below 0.8, covering all 8 factors.","Density suppression applies immediately to spawning via min(reproductive_readiness_index, density_factor), not gated behind the EMA lag.","Egg-dropping model uses both instability_pressure and temp_swing_pressure (max of both), capped at egg_drop_max_probability (named parameter), with event diagnostics identifying the trigger.","Four previously hardcoded condition constants are now named parameters: condition_do_reference_mg_l, condition_nh3_sensitivity, condition_nitrite_sensitivity, condition_hourly_stress_penalty_weight — each with defaults, invariants, preset exposure, and behavioral unit tests.","Preset validation test shrimp_preset_allows_zero_temp_condition_min_factor (presets.rs:3949) explicitly verifies that setting temp_condition_min_factor = 0.0 passes preset validation, confirming the amendment fix."],"findings_or_gaps":["Three warm-side temperature curve-shape constants (LOW_TEMP_REPRO_MIN_FACTOR=0.1, HIGH_TEMP_REPRO_SHOULDER_FACTOR=0.5, MIN_REPRO_SUPPRESSION_FACTOR=0.05) remain as file-level named constants rather than species parameters. Documented as intentionally fixed for the first-pass model (comment at shrimp.rs:1598-1600). The primary curve-width parameter (low_temp_repro_ramp_width_c) has been extracted. Acceptable for this deliverable — flagged in multiple prior review cycles and accepted each time.","The EMA smoothing for reproductive readiness is now a named parameter (reproductive_readiness_smoothing), resolving a gap flagged in cycle 2 round 1."],"follow_up_or_amendments":["If future tuning requires it, promote the three warm-side temperature curve-shape constants to ShrimpRuntimeParams. Low priority since they are well-documented named constants and the primary curve parameters are already tunable."],"outcome":"approved"},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"54133184-56a4-4a60-ab40-36aae96a8686"}
